# Docs usage

`docs/` is reference material for QA analysis — not source of truth for automation code.

- Start from `docs/README.md`; open sibling files only for the active question.
- When writing/updating tests: map to **one** `docs/test-cases/<area>.md`, then implement via existing page objects.
- Prefer `BUG_PATTERNS.md` / `BUSINESS_RULES.md` over the full exploratory catalog.
- Do not paste large doc sections into code comments; link the path instead.
- Automation code lives in `pages/`, `tests/`, `fixtures/`, `utils/` — docs do not replace those.
